WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.167
-George Lopez!
-Gracias!

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:04.133
-It is always great to see you,
my friend.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:07.234
-Yeah.
-You're such a funny, funny man.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:09.434
You were showing me something
backstage, by the way.

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:11.367
-Yeah.
-Can we talk about it here?

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.300
Something very --
very cool thing.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.634
This is --
-This --

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:16.067
[ Audience oohs ]
-Look at that.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:17.100
Yeah, show it off.
That's gorgeous.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.501
-This Rolex...
-Yeah.

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:22.501
...belonged to
the great Johnny Carson.

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:24.767
This is Johnny Carson's.

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:28.601
-Let me see this thing.
How did you --

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:30.033
-There was a jeweler
in Hollywood,

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:31.868
and it came into his possession,
and they thought,

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:34.033
"Well, you know, I think I might
know a guy that is interested."

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.434
You know, I love comedy.
I love the history of comedy.

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:37.701
-Of course.
-"The Tonight Show" --

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:39.133
I watched "The Tonight Show"
with Freddie Prinze,

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.901
Richard Pryor,
all my idols growing up.

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:43.667
-Yeah.
-And then, now you.

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.801
It was only right that the watch
come back to New York

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:48.133
and pay its dues right here
on "The Tonight Show."

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.901
-Come on, Johnny.

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:51.067
-Johnny.

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:52.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:55.901
-What year was that
when you were on with Johnny?

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.300
Do you remember?
-Man, you know what's crazy is,

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.200
it was -- it was November
of '91.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.400
-Is that right?
-So, then I'm 30 years old,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.634
and then I'm behind this curtain
here now,

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.501
and I'm 61 years old.

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:08.167
-Good for you, bud. Right?
-And, man, I made it back.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.167
So, yeah.

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:10.400
-[ Laughs ] Exactly.
-I made it back!

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.400
-No, you're alwa--
-Even though I look like --

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.067
even though I look like a
Mariachi and a wolf had a baby.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.501
-No, no, no, you do --

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:20.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:21.334
-You know what's crazy?

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:22.501
Before, when I left the hotel,
they're like,

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.400
"Hey, good luck on your show
Friday, Cheech."

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:26.667
-Oh, my God.

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:27.834
-"All right."

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:30.000
-Cheech. I'll take --
I'll take it.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.367
But, no, you always crush.

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:34.467
I remember seeing you
at The Improv and Laugh Factory

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:37.334
out in L.A. and, honestly,
you would never want to follow

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:39.501
George Lopez, because you --
the audience would

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.801
give you standing ovations
during the middle of your act.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.167
-They were all, you know,
Latinos.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.467
-No, no, no.

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:48.567
You crushed it every single time
I saw you, everywhere.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:49.901
You're always great.
-Oh, thank you, man.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.334
-And you're nice to me, too.
I'll never forget that.

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:52.701
-Absolutely.
You're a great guy.

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:53.734
-Thank you. Let's talk about
your new series,

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:55.033
"Lopez vs. Lopez."

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:56.834
Your co-star
is your real-life daughter.

00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:58.434
-My daughter, Mayan.
26 years old.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:00.234
-Mayan Lopez --
-I was divorced.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:02.667
And, then, you know, Mayan and
I didn't talk for a long time.

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:07.834
And she went on TikTok
to respond to a video

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:09.734
that someone made
attacking me.

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:14.767
And it was a video of her
twerking upside down.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.968
-Hm.
-And then, you know, I mean,

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:18.701
I realized I wasn't
the best dad,

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:20.200
but when your kid's twerking
upside down,

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.834
you've got some real [bleep]
problems.

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:24.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.367
You're like, "I didn't realize
it was this serious."

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.868
-Yeah, you got to --
you got to start -- yeah.

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:29.033
Yeah, wow, wow.

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:31.367
No, I understand.
No, I get -- yeah, I got it.

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:34.300
All right, well --
-I better get out there.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.400
I got to get out there.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.567
-Yeah, I've got to get out there
and start.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:40.267
But you said you said you've
been through therapy now

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:41.267
with your daughter.
-Yeah.

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:42.634
The therapy -- yeah, of course.

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:43.734
You know, because, you know,
you have to be responsible

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:46.434
for the trauma
that you've caused.

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:47.934
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.367
Where my grandmother would have
been like -- yeah, hey, right?

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:53.000
So, I -- I'm owning, for
the first time in my life,

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.334
my responsibility that --
to the marriage and as a father,

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:59.467
and, you know, as a -- you know,
to my daughter that I --

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.400
for the first time in my life,
I said, "Yeah, I'm responsible

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.968
for this, and I'm going to spend
the rest of my life

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:05.400
repairing it."
-Good for you.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:06.801
-And hopefully we can do it --

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:08.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:10.300
-Good for you.
-For seven years on NBC.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.467
-You didn't know it was
going to be a TV show.

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:15.300
-And then nobody will ever
see me again.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.667
No.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:19.701
-No, but -- but, you know,
if you think therapy is bad,

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:23.200
what's worse is
the elevator ride down after.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.033
Because it's all heavy stuff,

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:28.734
and then you're just
in the elevator --

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:31.167
You almost have to stagger out,
like when you dine and dash,

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:33.000
somebody goes out the back,
somebody goes out the front.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.167
-[ Laughs ] So, yeah, yeah.
Just leave right now.

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.501
Yeah, we're in --
-Don't go in the same car --

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:37.501
-No.
-When you're doing

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:38.534
trauma therapy.

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:39.734
And somebody just leaves
out the back,

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:41.100
and the other person's
just out the front --

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.634
-Yeah. Can we describe the show
any more than we have?

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:45.968
I mean, it's you
and your daughter.

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:47.567
-Yeah, me and my daughter.
And working it out.

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.968
Yeah. And, you know, the --
I live with them,

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.100
because after the pandemic,
you know,

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.367
I might have lost my business.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:54.133
So, it deals with --
the beginning of the episode

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.601
is where I start
to live with them.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:58.701
And that's why I look like this,
because there's only --

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:00.701
you can only go up from this.

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:01.734
-[ Laughs ] No, come on.

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:02.767
But it's generational.

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:03.901
It's also --
-It's generational.

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:05.334
And everybody will love it.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:08.067
And whether you have issues or
not, it's just really funny.

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:09.234
-Yeah.
-Yeah. And that's what we need

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:10.234
right now.
-Absolutely.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:11.400
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.200
Here's George Lopez
in "Lopez vs. Lopez."

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.400
Take a look at this.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.934
-I'm still not calling you
Chance,

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:19.067
because looks like there's a
chance that's not your father.

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:22.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:26.634
-Why would you say
something like that?

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:28.834
-Because the kid looks
very Mexican,

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:31.133
and you look like somebody
that wouldn't get a rose

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.167
on "The Bachelorette."

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:35.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:38.968
-Look, George, even though I'm
not the toxic Alpha male

00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:41.133
you wanted for Mayan's
life partner, I am confident

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:44.567
in who I am,
so you can't hurt me.

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:46.501
-Yeah, you broke eye contact
at the end there, bro.

00:04:46.501 --> 00:04:48.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.534 --> 00:04:49.601
-Dammit.

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:50.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:52.968
-That's exactly right.

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:55.267
George Lopez, everybody.

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:59.567
"Lopez vs. Lopez" premieres
this Friday at 8:00 p.m.

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:00.767
on NBC.

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:03.100
Cole Hauser joins us
after the break.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.267
Stick around, everybody!

00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:05.467
Johnny!

